DEVOPS SYSTEM DESIGN ROUND (FAANG-Style)

These questions test end-to-end thinking, not tools. Interviewers want to see how you design, reason, fail, recover, and communicate.

⸻

🏗️ DevOps System Design – High-Impact Scenarios
 1. Design a highly available, scalable web application on cloud with zero downtime deployments.
 2. How would you design a CI/CD platform that serves hundreds of teams?
 3. Design a Kubernetes platform for multi-tenant teams with security and isolation.
 4. How would you design observability (metrics, logs, traces) for a large microservices system?
 5. Design a disaster recovery strategy for a business-critical application.
 6. How do you design a secure secrets management system across environments?
 7. Design a cost-efficient architecture that can handle unpredictable traffic.
 8. How would you migrate a monolith to microservices safely?
 9. Design a multi-region deployment strategy with data consistency.
 10. How do you design infrastructure guardrails so teams don’t break production?
 11. Design a GitOps-based deployment model for Kubernetes.
 12. How would you design a self-healing system?
 13. Design a logging and audit system for compliance.
 14. How do you design networking for hybrid (on-prem + cloud) workloads?
 15. How do you measure DevOps success in an organization?

⸻

🧠 How Interviewers Evaluate Your Answer

They look for:
 • ✔ Clear assumptions
 • ✔ Trade-off discussions
 • ✔ Failure handling
 • ✔ Security & cost awareness
 • ✔ Communication clarity

Not:
 • ❌ Tool names
 • ❌ Perfect architecture diagrams
 • ❌ Buzzwords

⸻

🧩 Winning Answer Structure (Use This)

1️⃣ Clarify requirements
2️⃣ High-level design
3️⃣ Failure scenarios
4️⃣ Security & cost considerations
5️⃣ Trade-offs & alternatives
